Protons are ubiquitous in the physical world. Hence, studying their chemical properties is significant. Certain substances have a tendency to loss protons or gain protons, define the former as _acid_ and the latter _base_. This categorization is known as Brønsted-Lowry Theory. The specific case of the reaction taking place in aqueous solution is the Arrhenius Theory, where acid produces $"H"^+$ or $"H"_3"O"^+$ ions.
